//! edit.fussmode — F mode: the FUSS drawer over the live editor.
//!
//! Ports sagitta `src/mod/git/fussmode.c` (5,082 lines) and
//! `fussmode.h` (212) at 9ace98c2 under `s52-fuss-mode.md`, with the
//! drawer repairs of s56.5 §2–§4/§7 and s57.5–s57.7 and the FUSS menus'
//! seams of s57.13 (R-yw06-4 = A). The pure tree, navigation and
//! expansion are the `git` module's (`src/git/fusstree.lu`); this file is
//! the mode's state and lifecycle, its jump, its viewer and its
//! observers. The drawing is `fussdraw.lu`; the commands, prompts,
//! pickers and the commit flow are `fusscmds.lu`.
//!
//! C's shape and the port's:
//! - `ed->fuss` (a `FussMode *`) → `Ed.fuss`, a value built at `ed_new`.
//! - `Win *`/`Buffer *` held across calls (the viewer's, the commit
//!   view's) → window and buffer IDS, looked up when used.
//! - `ed->interner` path ids in `YEW_REGION_FUSS_ROW` payloads → F mode's
//!   own interner, `FussMode.paths` (only FUSS rows carry path ids).
//! - C's `FussPathRef` scratch of the open tabs' paths → `open_scratch`,
//!   a `git.GitPaths` reset and refilled per refresh (G33).
//! - C's `PickerSpec` callbacks → the picker's `PICK_HOST_FUSS` kind.

use git
use std.signal
use term
use text
use util
use ws

